{"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/laplacianeigenpairs(smallest:tolerance:maxiterations:)"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SpectralGraphTheory","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"laplacianEigenpairs"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"smallest","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tolerance","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxIterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV","text":"NoConvergence"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:19SpectralGraphTheory10EigenpairsV","text":"Eigenpairs"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method","title":"laplacianEigenpairs(smallest:tolerance:maxIterations:)","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P08SpectralA6TheoryE19laplacianEigenpairs8smallest9tolerance13maxIterationsAD0F0VyxGSi_SdSiSgtAA13NoConvergenceVYKF","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","role":"symbol","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SpectralGraphTheory\/Eigenpairs.swift#L332","fileName":"Eigenpairs.swift"}},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"laplacianEigenpairs","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"smallest","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tolerance","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = 1e-8, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxIterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"? = nil) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"NoConvergence","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Eigenpairs","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/Eigenpairs","preciseIdentifier":"s:19SpectralGraphTheory10EigenpairsV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"smallest","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The number of eigenpairs, in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0...vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"tolerance","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The residual a Ritz pair must reach, relative as described above."}]}]},{"name":"maxIterations","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The matrix–vector products each Lanczos run may spend; nil for the limits","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"under Throws.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The eigenpairs, in order from that end of the spectrum."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Component by component: each component’s null vector first (eigenvalue 0, components in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order of their least vertex), then the smallest positive eigenvalues of the components"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"merged. On a component of at least 64 vertices, thick-restart Lanczos (Wu–Simon) with full"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reorthogonalization and locking, the null vector projected out, from a fixed start vector:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on σI − M (σ Gershgorin’s bound) while σ\/λ₂ is moderate, else on M⁺ by shift-invert, each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"product a conjugate-gradient solve with L grounded at the vertex of largest degree. A Ritz"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pair is accepted when its residual is at most "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance"},{"type":"text","text":" · λ, relative to itself as for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"algebraicConnectivity"},{"type":"text","text":"; the vectors found are then rotated by Rayleigh–Ritz on M, and each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value is its vector’s Rayleigh quotient, a sum over edges. The dense solver on a smaller"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component, or when k is a third of it or more."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O((n + m) · products + n · k²) time, O(n · k) "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"s for the vectors and n · max(30, 2k +"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"10) for the basis."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"code":"smallest","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is in "},{"code":"0...vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"tolerance > 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when given, is at least 1."}]}],"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Precondition"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NoConvergence"},{"type":"text","text":" when a Lanczos run by shift-invert spends "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":" products"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(1,000 when nil), or a conjugate-gradient solve inside it 20,000 + 2n iterations, without"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"converging. A run on σI − M hands over to shift-invert rather than throwing, after 4,000 +"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"20√n products or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":", whichever is smaller. The dense solver throws as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"laplacianSpectrum"},{"type":"text","text":" does."}]}],"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Throws"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The k smallest eigenvalues of the Laplacian L ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"laplacianMatrix()"},{"type":"text","text":"), k = "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"smallest"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ascending, each with a unit eigenvector (see "},{"code":"Eigenpairs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/laplacianEigenpairs(smallest:tolerance:maxIterations:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/GraphProtocols":{"url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","title":"GraphProtocols"},"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Graph","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory","role":"collection","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"SpectralGraphTheory"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/NoConvergence":{"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/noconvergence","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"NoConvergence","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The error an iterative method throws when it uses up its iteration limit without meeting its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stopping rule."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"NoConvergence","k